From: Local NixOS bring-up <local@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 22:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sophgo: initialize secondary mux parent function

CV1800_GENERATE_PIN_MUX2 describes pads whose final function is selected
through a second mux.  The primary mux's final slot routes the pad to that
secondary mux, but the macro leaves mux2.pfunc zero-initialized.

cv1800_verify_pinmux_config() consequently rejects every useful PINMUX2()
setting because it requires the requested primary function to equal
mux2.pfunc.  All current users describe a seven-function primary mux and a
seven-function secondary mux, with primary function 7 selecting the second
mux.  Record that parent function from the primary mux limit.

This lets DT users select, for example, SG2002's MIPIRX4N function 7 and
then SPI1_SCK function 6.

Signed-off-by: Local NixOS bring-up <local@example.invalid>
---
 drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.h b/drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.h
index bd3f3ba5001b..3c9e24b4aa6a 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.h
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sophgo/pinctrl-cv18xx.h
@@ -118,6 +118,7 @@ static inline enum cv1800_pin_io_type cv1800_pin_io_type(const struct cv1800_pin
 			.area = (_mux2_area),				\
 			.offset = (_mux2_offset),			\
 			.max = (_mux2_func_max),			\
+			.pfunc = (_mux_func_max),			\
 		},							\
 		.conf = {						\
 			.area = (_conf_area),				\
